    "result_text": "All 300 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. (The `ERROR ExceptionControllerAdvice` line is a pre-existing log message from a UserRestController test that deliberately triggers an error \u2014 that test still passes.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field on owner creation. When an owner is created, the response now includes `locality` set to `\"local\"` if their city is the single most common city among existing owners at that moment, otherwise `\"remote\"`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` is regenerated from this at build time).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient locality` field with getter/setter, matching the existing pattern for `namesakeCount`/`sharesHousehold`.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, set `owner.setLocality(resolveLocality(owner.getCity()))` before persisting, and added the `resolveLocality` helper. It groups existing owners by normalized city, finds the highest count, and returns `\"local\"` only when exactly one city holds that max and it matches the new owner's city; ties, brand-new cities, and an empty owner set all yield `\"remote\"`. City matching reuses the existing `normalize` helper, so it's case/whitespace-insensitive like the rest of the controller.\n- MapStruct auto-maps `locality` (matching property names), consistent with the other computed fields.\n\nNew tests in `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests` cover: most-common city (`Madison` \u2192 local), case-insensitive match (`madison` \u2192 local), a less-common city (`Monona` \u2192 remote), and a brand-new city (`Boston` \u2192 remote).",
